# simple-gin smoke test. nvim + kulala.nvim.
# {{host}} from @host below. <Space>ra sends all, <Space>rr sends one.
# Captures use a post-request script (> {% %}) which stores the id
# in client.global under the name "product_id". Later blocks read
# it back with {{product_id}}.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Health check
GET {{host}}/healthz

### 1) Create a product — captures {{product_id}} from data.data1
POST {{host}}/product
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Espresso Beans 1kg",
  "description": "Single-origin Ethiopian roast",
  "sale_price": 24.50,
  "price": 29.90
}

> {%
  client.global.set("product_id", response.body.data.data1);
%}

### 2) Create a minimal product — overwrites {{product_id}} with the new id
POST {{host}}/product
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Plain Mug",
  "price": 9.99
}

> {%
  client.global.set("product_id", response.body.data.data1);
%}

### 3) List all products (sanity check the DB has data)
GET {{host}}/product

### 4) Get by id — {{product_id}} from #2 fills in
GET {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}

### 5) Patch by id — change only the price
PATCH {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 31.50
}

### 6) Patch by id — null out description and sale_price (explicit clear)
PATCH {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": null,
  "sale_price": null
}

### 7) Patch by id — invalid (negative price), expect 422 INVALID_PRICE
PATCH {{host}}/product/{{product_id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": -1
}

### 8) Patch a non-existent id, expect 404 PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND
PATCH {{host}}/product/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 1
}
